; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Business life-cycle (Phase 7). Only business_failure is authored here for
; now - the merit-gated founding events (business_founding / _partnership /
; investment) wait on the F3 derived-situations layer.
;
; business_failure is a ZERO-ROLE event: it has no per-entity role, so the
; engine fires it once each December with no role-enumeration walk in
; progress. The (fail-businesses ...) verb then collects every org and
; dissolves the failures. This ordering matters - dissolve_org destroys the
; org's document entities, and destroying an entity while a role-enumeration
; mx_for_each_entity is still walking corrupts that walk. (The same reason
; the engine emigrates only from the zero-role homeostat event.)
;
; v1 fails any org at a flat low rate; restricting to commercial orgs and
; modulating by employee count are refinements for later.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

(hsim-event business_failure
  (nl         "businesses fail in hard times")
  (kind       _business_failure)
  (schedule   (annually december))
  (rng-stream business)

  (effects
    (fail-businesses 0.02)))
